[center][size=5][b]Mod Warning Skip[/b][/size]
Skips the No Man's Sky "mods detected" warning dialog.[/center]

[b]What it does[/b]
The warning dialog is dismissed automatically, so you go straight to the Main Menu. Pair with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/games/nomanssky/mods/4706]Intro Skip[/url] to skip the startup logos too.

[b]Toggles[/b]
None - the single patch applies whenever the mod folder is present. Remove
the folder or set [i]enabled = false[/i] in [b]mod.toml[/b] to turn it off.

[b]Requires:[/b] the [b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/games/nomanssky/mods/4700]Nozavolochen Framework[/url][/b] (provides the shared host DLL - spec-driven, no closed-source loaders).

[b]Install[/b]
Install like any other mod into [b]GAMEDATA/MODS[/b] so you end up with [b]GAMEDATA/MODS/Mod Warning Skip/mod.toml[/b]. The Nozavolochen framework provides the host DLL. After launch [i]Binaries/nozavolochen.log[/i] shows what was applied or any errors.

[b]Compatibility[/b]
[list]
[*]Runtime memory patches applied by the host DLL at boot. No game files
are modified, so there is nothing to merge and nothing to conflict with[/*]
[*]Patterns are checked before patching - a game update that shifts them is
reported in the log instead of misbehaving[/*]
[/list]

Source: [url=https://github.com/SavageCore/nms-mod-warning-skip]https://github.com/SavageCore/nms-mod-warning-skip[/url]